```

Step 2: Write the JavaScript function to calculate the product of the prime numbers and update the DOM with the result.

```javascript
// app.js
const primes = [3, 7, 13, 19];
let product = 1;

function isPrime(num) {
    for (let i = 2; i <= Math.sqrt(num); i++) {
        if (num % i === 0) return false;
    }
    return num > 1;
}

for (const prime of primes) {
    if (isPrime(prime)) {
        document.getElementById('primes').innerHTML += `<li>${prime}</li>`;
        product *= prime;
    }
}
document.getElementById('product').innerHTML = `Product: ${product}`;
```

Step 3: Verify your code by opening the created HTML file in a web browser. The prime numbers will be displayed as list items within the container, and the product will be shown below them.

